---
export const title = 'Scrolling content';
export const order = 300;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  When the content is taller than the screen, only the body scrolls. The header and the
  footer actions stay in view. The page behind the modal does not scroll while it is open.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-button variant='outlined' data-open-modal='terms-modal'>Review terms of service</wc-button>

  <wc-modal id='terms-modal' heading='Terms of service' subheading='Updated 1 November 2026' size='lg' no-scrim-close>
    <h3 class='text-title-medium'>1. Your account</h3>
    <p class='modal-demo-text text-body-medium'>
      You are responsible for the activity on your account and for keeping your password safe.
      Tell us straight away if you think someone else has used your account. You must be at
      least 16 years old to create an account.
    </p>

    <h3 class='text-title-medium'>2. Your content</h3>
    <p class='modal-demo-text text-body-medium'>
      You keep ownership of everything you upload. You give us a licence to host, copy and
      display it only so that we can run the service for you and the people you share it with.
      The licence ends when you delete the content, apart from copies in backups, which expire
      within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h3 class='text-title-medium'>3. Acceptable use</h3>
    <p class='modal-demo-text text-body-medium'>
      Don’t use the service to break the law, to send spam, or to get around usage limits. Don’t
      probe, scan or test the security of the service without written permission. We may
      suspend an account that puts other customers at risk; we will tell you why.
    </p>

    <h3 class='text-title-medium'>4. Plans and billing</h3>
    <p class='modal-demo-text text-body-medium'>
      Paid plans renew each month or year until you cancel. When you upgrade, you pay the
      difference for the rest of the period. When you downgrade, the change starts at the next
      renewal. Prices exclude tax, which we add where the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h3 class='text-title-medium'>5. Availability</h3>
    <p class='modal-demo-text text-body-medium'>
      We aim for 99.9% monthly uptime and publish incidents on our status page. Planned
      maintenance is announced at least 48 hours ahead and does not count as downtime.
    </p>

    <h3 class='text-title-medium'>6. Ending the agreement</h3>
    <p class='modal-demo-text text-body-medium'>
      You can close your account at any time from Settings. You can export your data for 30
      days after closing; after that we delete it. We can end the agreement with 30 days’
      notice, or straight away if you seriously break these terms.
    </p>

    <h3 class='text-title-medium'>7. Liability</h3>
    <p class='modal-demo-text text-body-medium'>
      The service is provided as is. To the extent the law allows, our total liability is
      limited to what you paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these terms
      limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h3 class='text-title-medium'>8. Changes to these terms</h3>
    <p class='modal-demo-text text-body-medium'>
      We will email you at least 30 days before a change that affects you. If you keep using
      the service after the change takes effect, you accept the new terms.
    </p>

    <div slot='footer' class='modal-demo-actions'>
      <wc-checkbox id='terms-agree' label='I have read and agree'></wc-checkbox>
      <span class='modal-demo-spacer'></span>
      <wc-button variant='text' data-close-modal>Decline</wc-button>
      <wc-button id='terms-accept' disabled data-close-modal>Accept</wc-button>
    </div>
  </wc-modal>

  <script is:inline>
    document.getElementById('terms-agree').addEventListener('change', event => {
      document.getElementById('terms-accept').disabled = !event.target.checked;
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  This modal sets <code>no-scrim-close</code>, so a click outside it doesn’t dismiss it by
  accident. Escape and the close button still work.
</p>
